---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base lang="en" title="Manufacturing & Verification · ORDO">
  <section class="page">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="hero">
        <h1 class="h1">Manufacturing &amp; Verification</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Verifiable facts—so you can judge whether an instrument exists in reality and has entered a repeatable manufacturing and delivery flow.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions" aria-label="Related">
          <a class="btn" href="/en/releases">Software release facts</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/en/shop">Hardware store</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/en/support">Support</a>
        </div>

        <p class="note">
          Note: this page focuses on <strong>hardware</strong> manufacturing/verification. For software versions and changes, use the <a class="inline" href="/en/releases">Releases</a> page.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 class="h2">Materials</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="feature">
          <figure class="media">
            <img
              src="/images/evidence/materials/carbon-fiber-prepreg.png"
              alt="Carbon fiber prepreg (release film and backing paper)"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <figcaption>
              Carbon fiber prepreg: the film, backing paper, and weave are structural—no printing and no skin.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <div class="copy">
            <div class="k">Carbon fiber (current mainline)</div>
            <p class="p">
              The current line uses carbon-fiber composites to keep tactile and visual language consistent, and to support long-term desk presence.
            </p>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>Public material type and what batch range can be disclosed</li>
              <li>Public surface treatment principles for consistency</li>
              <li>Structural constraints that matter (layers, contact surfaces)</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="note">
              Materials are not beliefs. If future scenarios require heat resistance, skin-friendly surfaces, stain resistance, or food-grade materials, verifiability comes first.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 class="h2">Process &amp; Acceptance</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="grid">
          <figure class="card">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="k">Making</div>
              <div class="mini">in process / equipment &amp; environment</div>
            </div>
            <img class="img" src="/images/evidence/process-cnc.jpg" alt="CNC process (carbon fiber plate)" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption class="cap">Verify: made in reality—not rendered.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="card">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="k">Delivery logs</div>
              <div class="mini">batch / packing / stacking</div>
            </div>
            <img class="img" src="/images/evidence/delivery-batch.jpg" alt="Batch packaging and stacking" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption class="cap">Verify: repeatable manufacturing enters delivery flow.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="card">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="k">Acceptance</div>
              <div class="mini">measurement / inspection / re-check</div>
            </div>
            <img class="img" src="/images/evidence/inspection-qc.jpg" alt="Quality check and measurement" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption class="cap">Verify: structure &amp; consistency are checked—never “done and forget”.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="card">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="k">Durability &amp; care</div>
              <div class="mini">wear / surface behavior</div>
            </div>
            <img class="img" src="/images/evidence/longevity-surface.jpg" alt="Surface behavior (water beads on carbon fiber)" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption class="cap">Verify: long-term boundaries and maintainability.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

</section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>

    .hero{ padding-top: 10px; }

    .lead{ margin: 12px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.72); line-height: 1.75; max-width: 96ch; }

    .hero-actions{ margin-top: 14px; display:flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.note{ margin: 12px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.60); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 108ch; }
    .inline{ color: rgba(240,252,255,0.92); text-underline-offset: 2px; }

    .section{ margin-top: 14px; }
    .section-head{ display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-end; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

    .sublead{ margin: 6px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,0.66); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 100ch; }

    .feature{
      margin-top: 12px;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .media{
      margin:0;
      border-radius: 22px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(220,235,240,0.12);
      overflow: hidden;
      background: rgba(10,22,26,0.10);
      box-shadow: 0 18px 38px rgba(0,0,0,0.36), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      display:grid;
      grid-template-rows: 1fr auto;
      min-height: 320px;
    }
    .media img{ width:100%; height:100%; object-fit: cover; display:block; }
    .media figcaption{
      padding: 10px 12px;
      background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(0,0,0,0.55), rgba(0,0,0,0.0));
      color: rgba(220,235,240,0.88);
      font-size: 12px;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    }

    .copy{
      border-radius: 22px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(220,235,240,0.12);
      background: radial-gradient(120% 120% at 20% 0%,
        rgba(48, 92, 110, 0.24) 0%,
        rgba(14, 26, 30, 0.58) 44%,
        rgba(10, 16, 18, 0.36) 100%);
      box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0,0,0,0.36), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      padding: 18px;
    }
    .k{ font-weight: 800; color: rgba(220,235,240,0.92); letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 12px; }
    .p{ margin: 12px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.72); line-height: 1.75; }
    .list{ margin: 12px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; color: rgba(220,235,240,.72); line-height: 1.75; }
    .list li{ margin: 6px 0; }
    .note{ margin: 12px 0 0; }

    .grid{
      display:grid;
      /* 2×2 on desktop for readability */
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr));
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    .card-head{ padding: 12px 12px 10px; }
    .mini{ margin-top: 6px; font-size: 12px; color: rgba(220,235,240,.60); }
    .img{ width:100%; height: 220px; object-fit: cover; display:block; border-top: 1px solid rgba(220,235,240,0.06); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(220,235,240,0.06); }
    .cap{ padding: 10px 12px 12px; color: rgba(220,235,240,.70); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.65; }

    .footnote{ margin: 12px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.56); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.65; }

    @media (max-width: 1100px){
      .feature{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 680px){

      .grid{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .media{ min-height: 280px; }
      .img{ height: 200px; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
